# QA Quality Gate

A feature, screen, API, schema change, or workflow is **not done** until it
passes this gate. Attractive UI and compiling code are not evidence.

## Mandatory auditor

Before marking work complete, or before the final commit of a coherent unit
that changes product behaviour, invoke the **kima-qa-auditor** agent
(`.cursor/agents/kima-qa-auditor.md`) as a **read-only** pass.

The implementing agent must not audit its own work as a substitute. Treat the
auditor as independent: do not assume prior work is correct; do not equate
screens with working features.

## Source of truth (read in order)

1. `docs/PRODUCT_REQUIREMENTS.md` when present; otherwise the blueprint
   (`docs/blueprint/kima-compliance-os-blueprint-v1.0.md`) and
   `docs/foundation/*`
2. `docs/foundation/frontend-backend-coverage.md` for surface ↔ engine mapping
3. `CLAUDE.md` hard constraints
4. Relevant code, schemas, migrations, and tests

If requirements conflict, stop and report the conflict. If requirements are
missing, mark them UNDEFINED — never invent regulatory rules or imply unverified
tax rules are legally correct. Never claim DGI / Harmony integration.

## Gate criteria (all required)

A unit may only be marked done when the auditor's verdict is **PASS** or
**PASS WITH NOTES** with **no open P0 or P1**, and each of the following holds:

| Area | Required evidence |
|---|---|
| Product alignment | Business problem → user → feature → acceptance criteria mapped; FAIL/UNDEFINED called out |
| Frontend | Navigation, forms, validation, errors, loading, empty/offline, a11y, responsive (375/768/1024/1440), FR+EN parity; no decorative or misleading UI |
| Backend | Every user action traced through API / engine / storage / response; refusals surfaced with engine reasons |
| Data & security | Constraints, RLS, tenant isolation, roles, audit/events; no secrets; filing evidence-gated |
| End-to-end | Intended user can complete the task, or workflow marked **NOT TESTED** (code inspection alone is never PASS) |
| Coverage matrix | Updated in the same change when a surface is added or its backend binding changes |

## Severity → release

- **P0** — block commit of the unit to `main` until fixed (security, data loss, integrity, tenant leak)
- **P1** — block "done"; core workflow broken or high-risk defect
- **P2** — fix in the same unit when practical; otherwise track with owner and do not call release-ready
- **P3** — polish; may ship with notes

Never conceal blockers. Never approve unverified critical functionality.

## Verdict vocabulary

Every requirement under audit: `PASS` | `FAIL` | `PARTIAL` | `NOT TESTED` | `UNDEFINED`.

Do not mark PASS solely because code or a screen exists. Separate confirmed
findings from hypotheses. Do not fabricate tests, screenshots, files, or line
numbers.

## Remediation loop

For each confirmed FAIL/PARTIAL:

1. Implement the recommended correction (implementing agent — not the auditor)
2. Re-run **kima-qa-auditor** on the same scope
3. Only then commit and push (see always-commit-push)

## Out of scope for this gate

Docs-only typos, pure tooling under `.cursor/` that does not change product
behaviour, and explicitly labelled spikes may skip the full six-phase report —
still respect `CLAUDE.md` hard constraints and never invent tax/DGI claims.
